    "title": "Prescribed burns completed at 2 Houston parks, but some smoke or smell could be spotted: HFD - NewsBreak",
    "text": "8 hours ago\nThe Houston Fire Department announced it completed a prescribed burn at two Houston parks, but warned that some people could still see or smell smoke nearby as logs continue to smolder.\nHFD, in partnership with Houston wildlife officials, said the two burns were conducted at:\nTuesday, March 18: Sylvan Rodriguez Nature Preserve (1201 Clear Lake City Blvd.) Wednesday, March 19: Houston Arboretum & Nature Center (4501 Woodway Dr.)\nAuthorities said the prescribed fires were part of ongoing wildfire risk mitigation efforts.\n\"These operations reduce accumulated vegetation that could fuel dangerous wildfires while supporting the ecological health of this important natural area,\" HFD said on Facebook.\nWhile HFD said people will still see smoke or smell it nearby, they are monitoring the areas to ensure they don't pose a threat.\nFor more information, you can visit the city's website .\n2",
    "summary": "The Houston Fire Department announced it completed a prescribed burn at two Houston parks, but warned that some people could still see or smell smoke nearby as logs continue to smolder. HFD, in partnership with Houston wildlife officials, said the two burns were conducted at: Tuesday, March 18: Sylvan Rodriguez Nature Preserve (1201 Clear Lake City Blvd.) Wednesday, March 19: Houston Arboretum & Nature Center (4501 Woodway Dr.) Authorities said the prescribed fires were part of ongoing wildfire risk mitigation efforts.",
